4 CONC d H. Rose, 69, of South Main Street, a pipefitter for General Dynamics Electric Boat Division Groton, Conn. for 16 years, retiring in 1988, died Tuesday at Rhode Island Hospital after being stricken a
4 CONC t home. He was the husband of Lilly Amburn Rose.Born in Knoxville Tenn., a son of the late Robert L. and Bessie Ferrel Rose, he had been a Swansea, Mass resident for 25 years before moving to Warren e
4 CONC ight years ago. Mr. Rose served 23 years in the U.S. Navy, retiring in 1960, during which time he received the National Defense Medal, the American Campaign Medal, the AsiaticPacific Campaign Medal, t
4 CONC he World War II Victory Medal and several others. He was a member of the Pipefitters Union Groton, Conn.Besides his wife he leaves two sons Robert L. Rose Sr. of Middletown and Daniel Rose of Franklin
4 CONC , Mass; six daughters, Linda Rose of Wilmington, Del., Sharon Silvia of Swansea, Gloria Thompson of Bufford, Ga., Rebecca Adler of Sufrin, N.Y., Janelle Hart of Warwick, and Tracy L. Boehm of Johnston
4 CONC , and 10 grandchildren. The funeral will be held tomorrow at 10 a.m. in the Birchcrest Countryside Home of Waring-Ashton &amp; Coughlin-Sullivan-Driscoll, 189 Gardners Neck Rd, Swansea. Burial with Mi
4 CONC litary Honors will be in Mt Hope Cemetery Swansea.
