4 CONC Park, Kings Meadows, Tasmania, Australia&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Occupation: Cordwainer or Boot Maker&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Parents: &lt;a&gt;William Devey&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Susannah Catherine Phillips&lt;/a&gt
4 CONC ;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Wife: &lt;a&gt;Harriet Cunningham (born Boyd)&lt;/a&gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Children: &lt;a&gt;Albert Frederick Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Percy Harold Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&
4 CONC gt;Edgar John Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Mabel Alice Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Alfred Hedley Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Ruby Nerida Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Reginald James Cunningha
4 CONC m&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Arthur Leonard Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Doris Evalyn Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Thomas William Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Siblings: &lt;a&gt;Richard Davey&lt
4 CONC ;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;William Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Abraham Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Mary Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Catherine Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Alexander Cunningham&lt;/a&
4 CONC gt;, &lt;a&gt;James Cunningham&lt;/a&gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Additional information: &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;LifeSketch: John&#039;s birth father, it seems, was William Devey who died in
4 CONC  June 1865 when John was just 6 years old.  John&#039;s mother (Susannah Phillips) had left William Devey around 1859 and entered into a relationship with James Cunningham.  James and Susannah had 5 c
4 CONC hildren with the eldest being Abraham born on 21st February 1860.  John&#039;s birth record is elusive but the baptismal certificate attached to the 1868 Application for Admission to the Queen&#039;s 
4 CONC Orphan School for his brother William and half brother Abraham gives us a date of birth for John of 6th September 1858.  There are enough documents that support the family story that John&#039;s birth
4 CONC  father was William Devey and that he &#039;took&#039; the name Cunningham as a child about the time Susannah commenced her relationship with James.  The above mentioned application states that James 
4 CONC and Susannah (aka Susan) never married.  I have attached a source document to the record of John&#039;s brother [William Cunningham (LCJC-D99)] which consists of Digital Images (9 images) of file for 
4 CONC the Application for Admission to Queen&#039;s Orphan School at New Town (a suburb of Hobart, Tasmania, Australia) for William Davey (age 11 - incorrectly stated in the file to be 10 1/2) and his broth
4 CONC er Abraham Davey (aged 8).  The file contains some very useful information about their parents and siblings, including for John.  This includes:-  (1) that the parents are stated by James Cunningham a
4 CONC s being himself (which is not the case for William and John as their father was William Devey) and Susan Phillips (noted that her name was written as Davey which has then been crossed out), that James
4 CONC  Cunningham arrived in the colony of Tasmania on the ship &quot;Marion&quot; and that he was Free by Servitude on 13 March 1859 (meaning he was transported from Great Britain as a convict),   (2) the 
4 CONC boys names being shown as Davey by the Evandale (Tasmania, Australia) Police Officer who filled in the application dated 17 April 1868 whereas later in the file their surnames are listed as Cunningham
4 CONC  and also the boys are recorded as stating to the Orphan School authorities that their surname is Davey and not Cunningham,  (3) advice from the Evandale local officials that the parents were never ma
4 CONC rried, that the boys were baptised into the name Cunningham and other information including  (4) the reason for the application being that the parents stole a 5 pound note and were to be sentenced to 
4 CONC 24 months (James Cunningham) and 12 months (Susan Phillips) hard labour and that the parents subsequently were freed after serving their sentences and well able to look after their children.  There is
4 CONC  also a certificate attached to the file from Robert Russell, Presbyterian Minister of Religion in Evandale dated 17 April 1868 stating he baptised 4 boys on 27 August 1866, the children of James Cunn
4 CONC ingham and Susan Cunningham whose maiden name was Phillips.  The names (William, John, Abraham and Alexander) and birth dates of the boys are given.  Point (1) above notes that the claim by James Cunn
4 CONC ingham that he is the father of William and John is incorrect.  James lived with but never married William and Johns&#039; mother Susan (aka Susannah) Phillips.  Susan never married William Devey but 
4 CONC she took his name whilst living with him and then later took the name of Cunningham when she went to live with James Cunningham around 1859 and with whom she had further children.  To clarify, William
4 CONC  and Johns&#039; father was William Devey (name morphed to Davey) and the boys were only about 2 years and 1 year old when Susan presumably left William and went to live with James Cunningham whose na
4 CONC me, like their mother (Susan), they subsequently took on.  John married Harriet Boyd on 26th February 1878 in Lymington (near Evandale, Tasmania, Australia).  There was an article in the local newspap
4 CONC er (North Eastern Advertiser) in 1938 on the occasion of their 60th wedding anniversary that has useful information about John and Harriets&#039; lives including that which loosely fits the events of 
4 CONC John&#039;s early years.
