1 NOTE When Lucy came to the States, she worked in a home in Syracuse for a few years before she moved in with Hubert Burls.

Lucy Bray Burls, 78, widow of Bernard Burls, passed away Sunday morning, March 17
2 CONC , 1935 at the home of her son, Hubert Burls on Morris 

Street.

She had been living with Hubert for the last four years....

She was born in England, the daughter of Mr. & Mrs. Thomas Bray....


Mrs.
2 CONC  Lucy Burls, 78, widow of B&amp;lt; lard Burls, passed away Sunday norning, March 17, at 4 o'clock at he home of her son, Hubert Burls on Morris street. 

Mrs. Burls was born n England, the daughter o
2 CONC f Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Bray. 

For the past our years she has made her home vith her son, during which time she has been in declining health. 

Funeral services were Conducted from the home Tuesday aft
2 CONC ernoon at 2 o'clock Rev. D. W. McVeigh officiating. 

Burial was at Louisville. 

She is survived by her son Hubert of Norfolk and one daughter in England, also severel grandchildren.

The passing of 
2 CONC Mrs Burls will be deeply regretted by her many friends in this vicinity. 

Norwood news., March 20, 1935
