Hubert B. Burls, 67, of Norfolk died at 9:50 a.m. January 21, 1955 at his home after b
2 CONC eing ill four months. Burial was in the Louisville Cemetery. 

Barn in England June 15, 18B7, son of Bernard Lucy Bray Burls. Educated in England as a child, he moved to Canada in 1910, to Gouverneur 
2 CONC in 1915 and then to Norfolk in 1926. 

On Mar. 1, 1913 he and Ella Beckstead were married in Morrisburg, Ont. 

He had been employed in the Norfolk Paper Mill since 1926. Surviving are his wife, a son
2 CONC . Elwood, Syracuse; four daughters, Mrs. Edgar (Velva) Clary, Stockholm, Mrs. Earl (Liiy) Phillips, Mrs. John (NIna)Alden, Pa., and Miss Lola Burls, a student at Houghton College, and nine grandchildr
2 CONC en.

The Massena observer., January 24, 1955
